{
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;The proposed two storey side extension, with particular reference to the resultant width of the property; its proximity and poor relationship to the neighbouring property at no.3 The Spinney, and the lack of set in from the property’s side boundary; would create a cramped, awkward and poor quality design against the local pattern of development and a localised terracing effect. It therefore fails to effectively integrate with the property overall, and the wider streetscene contrary to the high-quality design aspirations of the National Planning Policy Framework (2024), Policies D3 of The London Plan (2021), Policy CS.1B of the Harrow Core Strategy (2012), Policy DM1 of the Development Management Plan Local Policies (2013) and the adopted Supplementary Planning Document: Residential Design Guide (2010).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;"
